diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 7765fed..8c1fcdb 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -56,6 +56,16 @@ Database-backed job queue (no Redis):
 
 Recurring tasks are declared in `config/recurring.yml`.
 
+### Webhooks
+
+Boards can have webhooks that get POSTed about what happens on them:
+
+- Every `Event` is relayed (`Event::Relaying`) to the active webhooks on its board that subscribed to its action, which creates one `Webhook::Delivery` per webhook and enqueues `Webhook::DeliveryJob` on the `webhooks` queue.
+- A delivery is posted exactly once: the job claims it (`pending` -> `in_progress`), so duplicate jobs and retries never post it twice, and failed deliveries are never posted again.
+- Every delivery logs the request headers it was sent with (the signature is redacted in the API) and the response it got back.
+- `Webhook::DelinquencyTracker` switches a webhook off after `CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES_LIMIT` (10) consecutive failures inside `FAILURE_WINDOW` (1 hour); reactivating it starts from a clean slate.
+- `Webhook::Delivery.cleanup` (recurring every 15 minutes) drops the log entries that are older than `RETENTION_PERIOD` (1 week).
+
 ### Sharded Full-Text Search
 
 Full-text search runs in the database, not Elasticsearch. On MySQL it is sharded 16 ways by CRC32 of the account ID (`Search::Record::Trilogy`); on SQLite it is a single FTS5 index (`Search::Record::SQLite`). Don't assume the sharded shape when working under SQLite. Models in `app/models/search/`.
